              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gary"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very authentic and true to the old recipe. Those of you who complain don't understand \"authentic\". Change it to your liking but quit harping, learn to cook and realize where the recipe originated. Bunch of dummies!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mo Mo2Ca Cal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Halušky. I’m Bohemian Czech. \n\nHalusky Kapustou / Noodles with cabbage\n\nWe’d add egg to the batter for the Halušky. \n\nCut or passed through a spätzle maker. Okey dokey!",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-29T17:10:52.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TAW"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Quick and easy. I like my cabbage a little spicy so added garlic, onion powder, salt and pepper. I didn't chop, but cut thinly. Next time, I'll try chopping. Didn't have any butter (couldn't believe that) so I cooked in olive oil. Was delish. I enjoyed the dumplings, they are the same dumplings I put in soup so they were good for me. Served with fried fish. Family enjoyed. Will make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-04T22:46:15.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AustinTxGal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "3 stars since I modified the recipe 2 different times. Seasoned the flour for the dumplings and boiled them in vegetable broth. Also, added finely chopped carrots to the cabbage (the recipe directions did not have the carrots as pictured) and seasoned the cabbage for more flavor. Used some of the broth from the boiled water for the dumplings in the cabbage.\nthe second time I used package gnoochi; boiled slightly before adding to the cabbage. Very good and healthy meal.",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-29T17:58:04.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So much better when you fry 6-8 slices of bacon til crisp and then use the bacon grease to fry the cabbage and onion. Crumble the bacon and add to the dish!",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-30T10:35:11.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hydes Cookin'"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Cabbage was great but dumplings needed some help. These create heavy dumplings. Lighter dumplings add more water.This is what I did: \n2 cups flour, 1 egg, 1/4 tsp salt, 1/3 cup water. I boil with lid on 10 min then lid off ten. The last step seems backwards but that's how my Grandma made them and they we perfect every time.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-17T16:46:36.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Erin Madar"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Major yums! I used less butter--about half a stick, I just couldn't bring myself to use as much as called for--and since some had said that the dumplings were bland and hard, I made a batch of spaetzel from the allrecipes recipe, which is made with egg and milk instead of water, and added that instead. I also added a teaspoon or so of caraway seeds while cooking the onions. Fantastic! Even my boyfriend who doesn't like cabbage had seconds.",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-31T10:00:19.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debbi Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "After reading reviews I used broth rather than water and seasoned the dumplings. I added lean ham as well. I think left overs will be even better.",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-03T00:01:54.500Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Erica Maciulewicz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I sauteed the cabbage and onions until golden brown adding a little salt at the end of the cooking time. Doubled the dumpling recipe and added a tsp of baking powder and a little salt. Boiled golf ball sized dumplings for 5 mins then lowered heat to low, covered and cooked another 5 mins before removing and adding to cabbage mixture.",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-30T08:59:11.103Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lahull23"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked the chewy dumplings. It sounded a bit plain, so I added some parsley flakes and a touch of onion powder to them, and cooked the cabbage with diced ham. When I eat it at work I always get people saying that it smells good!",
            "datePublished": "2022-01-10T14:24:13.943Z"
          },
